rom carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$"] [:db/cas 17592186237897 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186263030 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186263105 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186263515 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186263760 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -19 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -19 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186263800 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186263810 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1 \